  "text_md": "# SA SOLDIER\n\n![](<0b045ab838c05c4ff1ac844caf826f8f368d_page_2_pg1_images/imageFile1.png>)\n\nThe official monthly magazine of the SA Department of Defence\n\nFrom the Editor’s desk 4\n\nEnd of an era for the Executive National Security Programme 5\n\nLetters to the editor 6\n\nSouth Africa assists Mozambique Government during the floods 10\n\nMandela Commemoration Medal Parade 12\n\nChief SANDF bestows medals for first-class service to the SANDF 16\n\n![](<0b045ab838c05c4ff1ac844caf826f8f368d_page_2_pg1_images/imageFile1.png>)\n\n18\n\nNational Civic Remembrance Sunday and Wreath-laying Ceremony 18\n\nSA Army observes the 96 th anniversary of Armistice Day 20\n\nSTREET ADDRESS   Defence Headquarters cor Nossob & Boeing St Erasmuskloof PRETORIA    \n\nFuture Armour Capability Conference 22\n\nTraining Command bids farewell to its General Officer Commanding 24\n\nGraduation ceremony of the Joint Senior Command and Staff Programme 25\n\nChief Human Resources honours his loyal members 26\n\n7 th Warrant Officers’ Academy Certificate Ceremony 28\n\nMilitary Academy awarded its students who excelled 29\n\nMitchells Plain Festival 30\n\nPreparing SA youth for a nautical career 32\n\nA visit to Air Force Base Ysterplaat Museum 34\n\nRetire or resign with GEPF: What you need to know 36\n\n![](<0b045ab838c05c4ff1ac844caf826f8f368d_page_2_pg1_images/imageFile2.png>)\n\nJohannesburg Regiments Association exercises its Freedom of Entry in Soweto 39\n\nThe DOD participates in Chief SANDF Prestige Week 40\n\nDiseases of lifestyle pose a threat to the development of SA 42\n\nEmbracing our colleagues with disabilities 43\n\n# CONTRIBUTIONS:\n\nAlthough all possible care is taken with articles, the editorial staff cannot accept any responsibility for lost articles and photographs.\n\n# REPRODUCTION, PRINTING & DISTRIBUTION: Formeset Print (Pty) Ltd\n\n24 Kinghall Avenue EPPINGDUST, Cape Town, 7460 Tel: (021) 507 9000 Fax: (021) 506 9092 email: formeset@formeset.co.za\n\n2005 Winner of the Government Communicator of the Year Award (GCIS). 2005 Winner of the National Ubungcweti Award (GCIS).\n\nPOSTAL ADDRESS SA SOLDIER Private Bag X158 PRETORIA, 0001\n\n# TELEPHONE\n\nTel: (012) 355 6341 Fax: (012) 355 6399 email:sasoldier@mil.za website: www.dod.mil.za\n\nwebsite: www.dod.mil.za\n\n# EDITORIAL STAFF    \n\nEditor:\n\nMs Nelda Pienaar\n\nDeputy Editor:\n\nMr Lufuno Netshirembe\n\nEditorial Staff:\n\nS Sgt Lebogang Tlhaole Sgt Itumeleng Makhubela Cpl Ally Rakoma\n\nTranslation  \n\nConsultant:\n\nDirectorate Language Services\n\nDistribution:  \n\nMr Jim Tshabalala Tel: (012) 355 6341\n\nLayout & Design:   Mr Werner van der Westhuizen\n\n",
